# Old build URLs -> the current build.
# Beta was the published app link for the whole v0.9.9 run, Delta was live briefly,
# and Echo was the published link until v1.1. All are kept working for anyone who
# bookmarked them directly.
# 302 (not 301) on purpose: these are "whatever is current" aliases, and a 301
# would be cached permanently by browsers, making the next build swap unfixable
# for anyone who had followed the old link.
#
# These point straight at the current build rather than chaining through each other,
# so retiring the next version means editing the target, not untangling a chain.
#
# v1.0.0 is deliberately absent: it was built and deployed but never linked from the
# landing page, so nobody has it bookmarked. It stays reachable as a snapshot of the
# first self-contained build.

/theatrecueplayer_v0.9.9_beta       /theatrecueplayer_v1.1   302
/theatrecueplayer_v0.9.9_delta      /theatrecueplayer_v1.1   302
/theatrecueplayer_v0.9.9_echo       /theatrecueplayer_v1.1   302
/TheatreCuePlayer_v0.9.9_Beta.html  /theatrecueplayer_v1.1   302
/TheatreCuePlayer_v0.9.9_Delta.html /theatrecueplayer_v1.1   302
/TheatreCuePlayer_v0.9.9_Echo.html  /theatrecueplayer_v1.1   302
